  "title": "Sugar 100 Hz + bitter 40 Hz -> MN9 (taste competition)",
  "description": "Phase 5 competition experiment, the paper's Fig. 3b point. Two stimulus groups on the published model, map 630: the 21 right-side sugar taste neurons at 100 Hz and the 21 bitter taste neurons (the paper's list, sim/shiu_model.py BITTER_R_630) at 40 Hz. 1000 ms x 30 trials, seed 0. Both MN9 neurons are watched. Expected: MN9 (720575940660219265) drops from 67.6 Hz with sugar alone to 47.7 Hz here (paper: 45.3 Hz; our Phase 5 run with seed 0: 47.7 Hz). Bitter at 80 Hz takes it to about 13 Hz and at 120 Hz to about 1.4 Hz (docs/phase5-competition.md).",
